Bare with me ...

I remember playing a game called "Azure Dreams" for the PlayStation. 
It was a lot of fun and reminded me a lot of Nethack (except I played
that before I really knew that Nethack existed).  In the game, there
is a randomized tower with 40-some levels.  You go into the tower and
advance; the monsters get tougher on each floor, yada yada, you know
the drill.  But here's the thing: you can escape the tower by using a
Wind Crystal, which keeps all of your items.  Or if you die, you come
out of the tower minus all of your items.  Once you exit the tower you
go to a big town, which develops through the course of the game as you
find items in the tower that develop stuff in the town, etc.  Your
character never dies for good - as it can in Nethack - but each time
you go back into the tower you start over again at level one, and
whether or not you have any items is dependent on how you exited the
tower the last time.

I kind of like this game dynamic.  Instead of going through many
characters and not developing a very good attachment to any of them,
you get the chance to build up this one character gradually over time
throughout many different towers/dungeons.  Eventually, after going
into the tower enough times (and not losing your items by "dying"),
you have built up your items enough such that you can get all the way
to the top of the tower, finish off the boss, and beat the game.  The
game also had a really in-depth pet management/breeding system that is
much more in-depth than Nethack's.

Anyway, my thought is, death is pretty fundamental to Nethack, so
maybe that shouldn't be changed, but I think it'd be cool if the first
staircase you start on doesn't lead to an escape from the dungeon, but
rather, to a large town on the surface full of shops and stuff for
upgrading your equipment.  I think that'd be a lot of fun.

I also remember some Rogue variant from my childhood (I'm guessing it
was a rogue variant because it was played using ASCII characters much
like Nethack) which had a town on the top level with shops and from
there you'd descend into the dungeon.  Anyone know what I'm talking
about?

Anyway, I'm just wondering if someone has done this kind of a patch to
Nethack making the up staircase on level one leading to a city that
can be accessed throughout the game rather than the endgame which can
only be accessed with the Amulet.

